# grbl_dspic33ak128mc102.syms - `/opt/xc-dsc/bin/xc-dsc-nm --print-size --size-sort --demangle` on the committed RELEASE .elf.
# Plain-text, diffable: when a port's binary size drifts, `git diff` on this file shows WHICH function grew/shrank,
# not just that the binary changed. Regenerate with `python3 tools/build_artifacts.py build --platforms dspic33ak128mc102`.
# TOOLCHAIN DEFECT WORKAROUND: `/opt/xc-dsc/bin/xc-dsc-nm --print-size` only
# populates the size field for ~10% of this port's function
# symbols and, combined with --size-sort, silently DROPS every
# symbol it can't size instead of printing it with a 0/blank
# size (verified: `/opt/xc-dsc/bin/xc-dsc-nm --print-size --demangle` with no sort
# still omits the size field for the same symbols - this is
# nm's sizing, not the sort). Rows below tagged 'objdump
# addr-delta estimate' were recovered via `xc-dsc-objdump -t`/`-h`
# (address-delta to the next function, capped at the
# containing code section's end) instead - see platform.md
# 'known toolchain defects' and tools/build_artifacts.py
# gen_symbol_map()/_estimate_code_symbols().
